\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 21 Oct 2025]\nL9: # Title:DeepSeek-OCR: Contexts Optical Compression\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Haoran Wei , cite6†Yaofeng Sun , cite7†Yukun Li L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled DeepSeek-OCR: Contexts Optical Compression, by Haoran Wei and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We present DeepSeek-OCR as an initial investigation into the feasibility of compressing long contexts via optical 2D mapping. DeepSeek-OCR consists of two components: DeepEncoder and DeepSeek3B-MoE-A570M as the decoder. Specifically, DeepEncoder serves as the core engine, designed to maintain low activations under high-resolution input while achieving high compression ratios to ensure an optimal and manageable number of vision tokens.\nL17: Experiments show that when the number of text tokens is within 10 times that of vision tokens (i.e., a compression ratio < 10x), the model can achieve decoding (OCR) precision of 97%. Even at a compression ratio of 20x, the OCR accuracy still remains at about 60%. This shows considerable promise for research areas such as historical long-context compression and memory forgetting mechanisms in LLMs. Beyond this, DeepSeek-OCR also demonstrates high practical value.\nL18: On OmniDocBench, it surpasses GOT-OCR2.0 (256 tokens/page) using only 100 vision tokens, and outperforms MinerU2.0 (6000+ tokens per page on average) while utilizing fewer than 800 vision tokens. In production, DeepSeek-OCR can generate training data for LLMs/VLMs at a scale of 200k+ pages per day (a single A100-40G). Codes and model weights are publicly accessible at cite10†this http URL†github.com .\nL19: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2510.18234 [cs.CV]\nL21:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2510.18234v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL22:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.18234†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Haoran Wei [cite14†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Tue, 21 Oct 2025 02:41:44 UTC (7,007 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled DeepSeek-OCR: Contexts Optical Compression, by Haoran Wei and 2 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite8†View PDF L35:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite15†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite16†view license†creativecommons.org L39: \nL40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.CV\nL43: \nL44: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L45: \nL46: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2025-10 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite22†cs L51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (cite26†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL77: \nL78: Connected Papers (cite27†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL79: \nL80: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL81: \nL82: Litmaps (cite28†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL83: \nL84: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL85: \nL86: scite Smart Citations (cite2