Yu , cite18†Jianfeng Zhang , cite19†Yifan Zhu , cite20†Rui Chen , cite21†Jinxin Chi , cite22†Zixian Du , cite23†Li Han , cite24†Lixin Huang , cite25†Kaihua Jiang , cite26†Yuhan Li , cite27†Guan Luo , cite28†Shuguang Wang , cite29†Qianyi Wu , cite30†Fan Yang , cite18†Junyang Zhang , cite31†Xuanmeng Zhang L11: View a PDF of the paper titled Seed3D 1.0: From Images to High-Fidelity Simulation-Ready 3D Assets, by Jiashi Feng and 27 other authors\nL12: \nL13: cite32†View PDF cite33†HTML (experimental) L14: > Abstract:Developing embodied AI agents requires scalable training environments that balance content diversity with physics accuracy. World simulators provide such environments but face distinct limitations: video-based methods generate diverse content but lack real-time physics feedback for interactive learning, while physics-based engines provide accurate dynamics but face scalability limitations from costly manual asset creation.\nL15: We present Seed3D 1.0, a foundation model that generates simulation-ready 3D assets from single images, addressing the scalability challenge while maintaining physics rigor. Unlike existing 3D generation models, our system produces assets with accurate geometry, well-aligned textures, and realistic physically-based materials. These assets can be directly integrated into physics engines with minimal configuration, enabling deployment in robotic manipulation and simulation training.\nL16: Beyond individual objects, the system scales to complete scene generation through assembling objects into coherent environments. By enabling scalable simulation-ready content creation, Seed3D 1.0 provides a foundation for advancing physics-based world simulators. Seed3D 1.0 is now available on cite34†this https URL†console.volcengine.com L17: Comments:  | Seed3D 1.0 Technical Report; Official Page on cite35†this https URL†seed.bytedance.com L18: Subjects:  | Image and Video Processing (eess.IV); Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite36†arXiv:2510.19944 [eess.IV]\nL20:    | (or cite37†arXiv:2510.19944v1 [eess.IV] for this version)\nL21:    | cite38†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.19944†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Zhongcong Xu [cite39†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Wed, 22 Oct 2025 18:16:32 UTC (32,000 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Seed3D 1.0: From Images to High-Fidelity Simulation-Ready 3D Assets, by Jiashi Feng and 27 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * cite32†View PDF L34:   * cite33†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite40†TeX Source L36: \nL37: cite41†view license†creativecommons.org L38: ### Current browse context:\nL39: \nL40: eess.IV\nL41: \nL42: cite42†< prev |   cite43†next > L43: \nL44: cite44†new | cite45†recent | cite46†2025-10 L45: \nL46: Change to browse by:\nL47: \nL48: cite47†cs L49: cite48†cs.CV L50: cite49†eess L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite50†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite51†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite52†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (cite53†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Connected Papers (cite54†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL80: \nL81: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL82: \nL83: Litmaps (cite55†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL84: \nL85: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL86: \nL87: scite Smart Citations (