ence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL152: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite68†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL153: \nL154: cite69†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite70†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL155: \nL156: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite71†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL157: cite72†About†info.arxiv.org · cite73†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite74†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite75†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite76†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite77†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite78†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite79†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L158: \nL159: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2510.11370v1] Stabilizing MoE Reinforcement Learning by Aligning Training and Inference Routers (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.11370v1)\nciteturn2939view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.11370v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 13 Oct 2025 (this version), latest version 21 Oct 2025 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:Stabilizing MoE Reinforcement Learning by Aligning Training and Inference Routers\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Wenhan Ma , cite7†Hailin Zhang , cite8†Liang Zhao , cite9†Yifan Song , cite10†Yudong Wang , cite11†Zhifang Sui , cite12†Fuli Luo L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Stabilizing MoE Reinforcement Learning by Aligning Training and Inference Routers, by Wenhan Ma and 6 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite13†View PDF cite14†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Reinforcement learning (RL) has emerged as a crucial approach for enhancing the capabilities of large language models. However, in Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models, the routing mechanism often introduces instability, even leading to catastrophic RL training collapse. We analyze the training-inference consistency of MoE models and identify a notable discrepancy in routing behaviors between the two phases.\nL17: Moreover, even under identical conditions, the routing framework can yield divergent expert selections across repeated forward passes. To address this foundational inconsistency, we propose Rollout Routing Replay (R3), a method that records routing distributions from the inference engine and replays them during training. R3 significantly reduces training-inference policy KL divergence and mitigates extreme discrepancies without compromising training speed.\nL18: Extensive experiments on various settings confirm that R3 succeeds in stabilizing RL training, preventing collapse and outperforming methods such as GSPO and TIS. We believe this work can offer a new solution for stabilizing RL in MoE models.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2510.11370 [cs.CL]\nL21:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2510.11370v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\n"
